1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,780
Have you ever found yourself watching a trashy film on an aeroplane, tears welling up as the cheesy crooner sings its theme song?
你有没有发现自己在飞机上看一部蹩脚电影时，随着蹩脚的流行歌手演唱主题曲而热泪盈眶？

2
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:13,790
I certainly have.
我当然有过。

3
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:15,210
And I’m not alone.
而且不止我一个人这样。

4
00:00:15,210 --> 00:00:26,910
So much so that Virgin Atlantic recently released a list of the films that cause people to cry the most.
以至于维珍大西洋航空公司最近发布了一份最让人落泪的电影名单。

5
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:42,090
Get this: 7% of people admitted to crying during the sad parts, while 10% owned up to getting emotional at happy endings.
听听这个：7%的人承认在悲伤情节时哭过，而10%的人承认在幸福结局时情绪激动。

6
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:53,200
What is it about being 35,000 feet up in the air that causes such heightened emotions?
在35000英尺的高空，是什么导致了如此强烈的情绪呢？

7
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,580
So, what’s going on?
那么，这是怎么回事呢？

8
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:58,680
How does air travel tap into our hidden emotions?
乘坐飞机旅行是如何触动我们隐藏的情感的呢？

9
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:05,790
A study from the Netherlands has shown adults cry due to feelings of separation, loneliness or powerlessness.
荷兰的一项研究表明，成年人会因为分离、孤独或无力感而哭泣。

10
00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:14,240
All of these are easily experienced when flying: you‘re far from family, often alone, and have no control over the aircraft’s flight.
在飞行时，这些感受都很容易体会到：你远离家人，常常独自一人，而且无法控制飞机的飞行。

11
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:17,640
Another theory relates to the lack of distraction.
另一种理论与缺乏分散注意力的事物有关。

12
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:22,780
When you‘re strapped into your seat in a sealed cabin in the sky, there’s not a lot you can do.
当你被捆绑在天空中一个密封的客舱里的座位上时，你能做的事情并不多。

13
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:27,360
So we are able to invest ourselves more fully into the movies we watch.
所以我们能够更全身心地投入到我们所看的电影中。

14
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,560
Then there‘s the physical space.
然后是物理空间的因素。

15
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:34,080
Air pressure and oxygen levels are lower, and this can affect our mental state.
气压和氧气含量较低，这会影响我们的精神状态。

16
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:38,930
Conditions in an aeroplane resemble those at an altitude of 2,400m.
飞机内的环境类似于海拔2400米处的环境。

17
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:42,590
The reduced oxygen at this height can affect the brain.
在这个高度氧气含量的降低会影响大脑。

18
00:01:42,590 --> 00:01:50,600
According to a study by the US Institute of Medicine: “the initial mood experienced at altitude is euphoria, followed by depression.”
根据美国医学研究所的一项研究：“在高海拔地区最初的情绪体验是兴奋，随后是抑郁。”

19
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,630
And what about the movies themselves?
那么电影本身呢？

20
00:01:52,630 --> 00:02:01,860
Virgin say top culprits include tearjerkers such as Billy Elliot, Eat Pray Love and, at number one position, Toy Story 3.
维珍航空公司表示，最让人落泪的电影包括《跳出我天地》、《美食、祈祷和恋爱》，排名第一的是《玩具总动员3》。

21
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:11,100
Their emotional firepower even caused the aeroplane to slap tongue-in-cheek “emotional health warnings” on select movies back in 2011.
这些电影的情感冲击力甚至使得航空公司在2011年对某些电影半开玩笑似的贴上了“情感健康警告”。

22
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:20,160
Virgin Atlantic film critic Jason Solomons said at the time, “On a flight, we‘re isolated, leaving loved ones or aching to be reunited with them.
维珍大西洋航空公司的影评人杰森·所罗门斯当时说：“在飞行途中，我们与世隔绝，离开了所爱的人，或者渴望与他们团聚。

23
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:29,520
We’re nervous, we‘re tired, we might have had a drink at a time we usually wouldn’t, and if we see an image, a scene that reflects our emotional state, frankly we‘re suckers.
我们紧张、疲惫，我们可能会在平时不会喝酒的时候喝上一杯，如果我们看到一个画面、一个反映我们情感状态的场景，坦率地说，我们就变成容易被骗的傻瓜。

24
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,680
Flying and films is a heady cocktail.
坐飞机看电影就像喝了一杯令人陶醉的鸡尾酒。”
